# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets — never commit anything that could capture a real bot token or a
# live plugin configuration. The token is stored unencrypted in Dalamud's
# config folder; keep it off the repo entirely. (Plan §10)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.token
*.secret
secrets.*
appsettings.*.json
MaplesEcho.config.json
**/DalamudConfigs/**
**/pluginConfigs/**
config.local.*

# Build output
bin/
obj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
*.user
*.suo
.vs/
.idea/
*.DotSettings.user

# Packaged artifacts (built locally)
dist/
*.zip
# ...except the distribution zip the custom repo serves. This is committed so
# the custom-repo install/update links resolve without a GitHub Release. Rebuild
# and re-commit it on every version bump. (A GitHub Release is the cleaner
# long-term host if you'd rather keep binaries out of git.)
!repo/latest.zip
!repo/testing.zip

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
